cff-version: 1.2.0
title: StackAnt
message: >-
  If you use this software in published work, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Francesco Simone
    family-names: Mensa
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7374-4591'
abstract: >-
  StackAnt is a cross-platform PyQt6 desktop application that turns a
  manual-focus-pull video of a specimen into a focus-stacked composite
  image, aimed at entomologists doing macro photography. It extracts
  frames with ffmpeg, automatically rejects motion-blurred transition
  frames by Laplacian variance, and stacks either with an in-process
  Laplacian-pyramid method or the focus-stack CLI.
keywords:
  - focus stacking
  - macro photography
  - entomology
  - myrmecology
  - computational photography
  - image processing
  - scientific imaging
  - PyQt6
license: MIT
